---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Clear quantities before a busy trading day." description="A starting point for packaged food sellers with countable products.">
<PageHero eyebrow="The Kora product plan" title="Clear quantities before a busy trading day." lede="A starting point for packaged food sellers with countable products." />
<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 prose-kora">
<h2>Begin with defined packs</h2>
<p>Record a bag, sealed pack or carton as a defined variant. Confirm quantity and unit before taking an order.</p>
<h2>Be honest about specialist needs</h2>
<p>Batch tracing, expiry dates, temperature controls, weight-based selling and recipe ingredients are not part of the first inventory release. Merchants who depend on them need those features validated before relying on Kora.</p>
<h2>Test the core workflow first</h2>
<p>Opening stock, receiving, reservations, payments and dispatch are the initial focus. The pilot should match the actual goods and process being tested.</p>
<p><a href="/pilot" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the founding pilot</a></p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
